2026-09-25 M8 Signal Lab: the panel scores each company-month with the live code (pipeline.signals.weekly.score_company over registry.SIGNALS, context c1/c2/c3, scores.gap), fed by point-in-time cursors that give exactly the rows as_of(month-end) returns; cross-sections (S8 deciles, S12 sector medians, legacy thresholds, C3) are over the month's population (see the R2-F1 line). C4 (GDELT) has no history: Gap uses the C1-C3 available. C1 reads month-end multiples with at least 12 months of history (the weekly run's 52 weeks).
2026-09-25 M8: an event is a fire with no event for that company and signal in the previous 12 months (a signal that keeps firing gives one event a year). Excess = forward price return minus the equal-weighted mean of the month's population priced at both dates.
2026-09-25 M8: Newey-West on events = Bartlett weights over month distances (lags = horizon) on the monthly sums of residuals. With lags up to a third of an 84-month period the estimate is noisy and can fall far below the plain standard error by chance (F-LAB noise signal: t -5.2 vs -1.4), so t_nw uses the larger of the two SEs: the §4.10.5 rule never acts on a variance the data can't support. The prove-first lower bound (mean - 1.645 SE, audit §4.9) is stored in lab_results.notes.
2026-09-25 M8: Stooq's bulk closes are split-adjusted; market caps put each share count on the same basis with the splits found in the company's first-reported share counts (M4's share_splits); a detected split ratio changes no value, so it leaks nothing; a missed one (a ratio outside splits.RATIOS, or one hidden by issuance) would. 52-week highs and lows use month-level highest/lowest closes.
2026-09-25 M8: §4.10.5 proposals read the 12-month horizon (config/lab.yaml proposal_horizon_months); an S signal with no out-of-sample events gets the neutral 1.0, a legacy L signal stays 0. The proposal rewrites only the changed weights and the version line of config/weights.yaml; lab.yml opens that as its own PR (protected: human-approved label) and the report as another. L5 (small-cap momentum, $2B) applies to the US only.
2026-09-25 M8: F-LAB is generated in memory by fixtures/lab/make_lab.py (seed 7): the planted signal is the live S1 (a 40% order-book step, then +2.5% a month for 12 months), the noise signal the live S5 (a 4% buyback, no price effect); in-sample 2015-2016, out-of-sample 2017-2018 by event month.

