2026-09-25 M5 prompts: the P-0X system and user templates are text files copied verbatim from §5 / Appendix F.7 (tests/llm/test_prompts.py compares them); P-01/02/03/05 force a tool call, P-06/07 ask for JSON with a response schema. The brief gives no user message for P-06 and P-07: theirs are the simplest ones that carry the inputs (SPEC_ISSUES 24).
2026-09-25 M5 router: providers in config/quotas.yaml `routing` order; a 429 blocks that provider for its Retry-After, else until the next UTC day, and the next one is tried; any other failure also moves on; all out -> Deferred. Today's usage is read back from llm_calls, so a second run the same day doesn't overspend. A provider whose requests_per_day is null is unavailable; requests per minute are paced on the (injectable) clock; a request is estimated at 4 characters a token before the call.
2026-09-25 M5 privacy: the router takes only PublicData values (frozen dataclasses defined in pipeline.llm, pipeline.facts, pipeline.capex, pipeline.india.triage or pipeline.thesis.evidence_pack), checked field by field, recursively; anything else raises PrivacyViolation before a request is built. No private type has to be named, so a new private table can't be forgotten.
2026-09-25 M5 cassettes: one JSON file per request, keyed by a sha256 of the whole request (provider, model, prompt, texts, schema, mode, temperature), under pipeline/llm/cassettes/<prompt>/ with MANIFEST.sha256; a request that wasn't recorded is a provider error ("cassette miss"), never an old answer. record-cassettes.yml (manual) records F-SYN with the free keys and opens a PR.
2026-09-25 M5 text engine (Appendix F.3-F.4): canonical text as F.3 (NFC; zero-width characters dropped; "\n" inside a paragraph, "\n\n" between); hidden elements and ix:header dropped; tables as `cell | cell` rows; a section keeps its longest span (the table of contents repeats headings). 10-K/10-Q chunks cover MD&A and the F.3 notes (whole document minus Item 1A when no MD&A heading is found); 10k-token chunks (4 characters a token), 400 overlap. Prefilter: word-bounded keywords with an optional plural, all-caps ones (AI, MW, GW, GPU) case-sensitive.
2026-09-25 M5 grounding and Verify-1: exact match, else whitespace/punctuation-insensitive (letters, digits, symbols such as $, and % must match: % is kept although Unicode files it as punctuation, M5 review R1-F10), never fuzzy; the stored quote is the canonical text at the offsets. A number matches as written or scaled within the last reported digit, and the stored value is always the parsed one. Per-share amounts (EPS, "per share") count as share-price facts (V1-TYPE). An unknown subject_key becomes other:<slug> and goes to needs_review; capex keys take the resolved fiscal year (capex_guidance:FY2027).
2026-09-25 M5 periods: fiscal year N ends in calendar year N on the company's fiscal year end (SEC submissions fiscalYearEnd; India 0331); quarters and halves are 3- and 6-month blocks from the fiscal year's start; two-digit years are 20xx.
2026-09-25 M5 diffs (F.6): computed by code. A P-01 withdrawal is stored as `changed` with the note "withdrawn" (the diffs kinds have no withdrawn; SPEC_ISSUES 21). Risk diffs: 10-K to 10-K and 10-Q to 10-Q only; a 10-Q Item 1A that only points back to the 10-K isn't compared; a change is kept only with at least one allowed P-03 tag; the stored excerpt (<= 25 words) is the sentence that changed most, chosen by code.
2026-09-25 M5 deferral: a document is read all or nothing. When any of its P-01 calls defers, none of its facts are kept and the whole document is read again the next day (a partly read document would look like a document without those facts).
2026-09-25 M5 daily text run: scope in config/quotas.yaml work order (capex desk, then the top 100 of the latest shortlist without text facts, then live theses); SEC 10-K, 10-Q and 8-K items 1.01, 2.02, 2.03, 7.01, 8.01 (EX-99.1/EX-99.2, and the 8-K itself for 1.01/2.03) filed in the last 400 days for a company's first run; India: P-07 on 3 days of announcements, read_pdf ones queued. At most 40 documents a day while documents_per_day is null, and no document starts after 8 minutes (§2.5 budget; daily.yml `text` job).
2026-09-25 M5 links: P-02 picks from the top 5 rapidfuzz token_set_ratio candidates (SEC company list plus existing entities) in batches of 20 names; no pick creates an entity of P-02's kind; the fact type's relation links the fact's company to it.
2026-09-25 M5 demand index: YoY = level(t) / level(t - 52 weeks) - 1, point in time from verified facts published by t (summed inputs compare only the companies present at both dates); z against the input's own weekly YoY over 156 weeks (>= 12 values, spread >= 0.005, else no z); category value = mean z of its inputs; direction rising >= +0.5 sigma, falling <= -0.5 sigma, else flat. Facts older than 400 days no longer set a level (config/categories.yaml `index`).
2026-09-25 M5 memberships: US proposals from config/categories.yaml industry_map (capex-desk companies by Appendix H seed group, other ledger companies by SIC); India by P-06 on the company's announcements (365 days) and the latest annual report's prefiltered pages, every 90 days, at most 20 companies a week; each category needs a grounded quote. Everything starts `proposed`; a rejection needs a reason; only `confirmed` counts for S11.
2026-09-25 M5 graph and S11 view: anchors (hyperscalers) are distance 0; breadth-first over companies with entities as the hinges (same CIK or normalized name); S11 reads confirmed memberships, the latest index on or before W, the distance, and export exposure (two rising export-share facts, or an overseas order-book fact under a year old; the bonus when a verified export quote names the US or data centers).
2026-09-25 M5 EIA: planned units (status P, L, T, U, V, TS) of the monthly EIA-860M inventory, nameplate MW summed per month, 5 years back; the key only in the query string, never in an error message; fixtures/eia is the documented shape (SPEC_ISSUES 23).
2026-09-25 M5 workflows: daily.yml `text` after the SEC and NSE event jobs; weekly.yml `capex` (index, memberships) before `scores` and `capex_brief` after; size_guard after all of them. Migration 0009 (text facts, Capex Desk) follows M4's 0008.
