2026-09-25 M5 review R3-F3/F4: the per-share check reads the number's own clause; "2026 through 2028" and "FY2026-FY2028" are multi-year (no period), "FY26-27" is FY2027 for a March year end, and a two-year label is one fiscal year only when the year ends before December.
2026-09-25 M6 pack ids: quarterly values m:<metric>:<period_end>, ownership m:<field>:<quarter_end>, insider events m:insider:<uuid>, kill-criteria metrics m:<name> (their current value, e.g. m:revenue_ttm_yoy, m:signal:S1 = S1's strength), facts f:<uuid>, fired signals and non-clear red flags s:S1 / s:R2, context c:C1..C4, c:evidence, c:gap. A kill criterion names one of the pack's kill-criteria metrics; kill_criteria.py recomputes it with the same code (evidence_pack.kill_value).
2026-09-25 M6 pack contents: 12 quarters of revenue, operating and net income, CFO, capex, FCF (computed), RPO, debt, cash, equity and share counts; 8 quarters of ownership; the year's insider events (at most 20, newest first); the 20 newest verified facts whose document was published before the week's cutoff (thesis_repo.pack_facts applies pit's rule), links whose fact was published before it, confirmed capex categories; the week's scores, fired signals, non-clear red flags and context rows. Extra fields are refused, so nothing else can enter.
2026-09-25 M6 next filing window: the quarter after the latest known one; US 10-Q within 45 days of its end, 10-K (the fiscal year's last quarter) within 90; India results within 45 days, 60 for the fiscal year's last quarter; a window already closed moves on a quarter. A kill criterion's check_after must be after it.
2026-09-25 M6 validate.py numbers: every figure written with digits in a fact or why-mispriced sentence must equal a value under a cited id, or a difference, ratio or change of two cited values, within half a unit of the last digit written; a percent also compares with a ratio x 100. Years (1900-2100 without a currency or unit), dates, fiscal labels (FY2026, Q2, H1), form names (10-Q, 8-K, Item 2.01) and names like S1/C2 are labels; number words ("one of") are not figures. In assumptions and inferences a figure needs "(assumed)" within 25 characters after it.
2026-09-25 M6 validate.py kill criteria: the metric is one of the pack's kill-criteria metrics and has a value there; `changes` takes no threshold and triggers when the value differs from the pack's (the baseline); other operators need a threshold the pack value doesn't already meet (a criterion true on day one is not a kill criterion).
2026-09-25 M6 P-05: run on fact and why-mispriced sentences without figures (the number check confirms the rest). Without a provider (the routine's `make thesis-validate` runs offline) it is skipped with a note; thesis-ingest.yml, which has the free keys, checks again.
2026-09-25 M6 ingest: one generated card per company and week (migration 0010's unique index on theses(company_id, created_week) for routine/fallback); a re-run replaces a card still in `research` with its kill criteria and leaves one Manzoor already accepted or dismissed alone. The weeks come from the push event's added and modified paths under data/thesis_cards/.
2026-09-25 M6 fallback: from Monday 06:00 UTC after the week's Friday, and only when the week has no generated card; P-04 with the Gemini `card` model (routing key P-04-fallback), at most 2 attempts per card, each validated like the routine's (P-05 through the same router); cards go to the database only.
2026-09-25 M6 kill criteria: evaluated in weekly.yml's `thesis` job after scores (the week's fundamentals, ownership and signal rows are in by then) for theses in state thesis or position, from check_after on; a metric that can't be computed is `unknown`; a newly met condition dates the criterion (triggered_week), moves the thesis to review and lists it in the digest.
2026-09-25 M6 digest: stored in `digests` (the web Home reads it) and posted as the issue "Doomberg weekly — <ISO week>" (a re-run edits it; found by title among `digest`-labelled issues). Company links use the APP_URL repository variable when set. A source reads "late" after 3 days without success (sec, nse, llm) or 8 (stooq).
2026-09-25 M6 review R1-F2: card sentences cover the whole text: a line break, or . ! ? (with closing quotes) followed by a space or a capital ends one, except after an abbreviation (Corp., Inc., U.S., an initial) or inside a number; a citation-only segment joins the sentence before it.
2026-09-25 M6 review R1-F3/F8: a card figure (digits, or a number word with a unit) must equal, with its sign, a cited value or a delta between two cited periods of the same metric (later minus earlier, change, ratio); a percent compares with a value x 100, and with the raw value only for a `percent` unit. Direction words set the sign; "to X from Y" must go from the earlier period to the later one, with a verb that matches. Only [m|f|s|c:...] citations are removed; four-digit numbers alone are years; "June 30, 2026"-style dates are labels; "27.6% to $1.25 billion" is not a range (numbers._ranges needs matching kinds).
2026-09-25 M6 review R1-F4/F7: thesis-ingest.yml runs main's code against main's queue files and takes only data/thesis_cards/** from the pushed commit; a push that changed any other path ingests nothing. Every pack passes EvidencePack.model_validate before validate.py and P-04 (CardInput holds the EvidencePack; privacy.check accepts pydantic models defined in public modules, field by field). card_md is always the rendering of the validated JSON.
2026-09-25 M6 review R1-F5/F6: the weekly queue commit runs only on refs/heads/main, stages data/thesis_queue/ alone and pushes on top of a fresh origin/main (rebase, 3 tries); the digest is its own job that runs every week (always()), and says when the week has no scores.
2026-09-25 M6 review R1-F9/F10/F11/F12/F13: the fallback and ingest routers log to llm_calls and start from the day's usage (facts_repo.logged_router); a kill criterion's triggered_week moves when it goes from not met to met again; hype words match after folding case, apostrophes, hyphens and spacing; the digest opens with a banner of stale or late sources, with SLAs from config/staleness.yaml (§2.7: US weekly 8 days, India weekly 10); record-cassettes.yml records fallback P-04 on F-CARD's pack and its P-05 calls (pipeline.thesis.samples), and M6-04 replays them (BLOCKED(key) until recorded).
2026-09-25 M6 review R2-F1: a card sentence ends at any line break (\r, U+2028 too), and at ., ! or ? before a space, an opening bracket or quote, or a capital; after Corp., Inc., U.S., etc. and month abbreviations only when a capital follows; never after Mr./Dr./No./vs./e.g. or an initial of a name (John A. Smith, J.P. Morgan).
2026-09-25 M6 review R2-F2: direction words after a figure ("a 27.6% decline", "44.8% lower") and more fall verbs (plunged, slumped, tumbled, ...) give a figure its sign; "from Y to X" is checked like "to X from Y"; "doubled", "tripled", "halved", "threefold", "up by half" need a cited ratio (later / earlier) within 5% ("more than": at least it; "nearly": up to 15% below). Checked by code, so a card can't pass by leaving them to P-05.
2026-09-25 M6 review R2-F3/F4: fiscal labels no longer take the figure after them (Q2 45%), signal names are capitals only (S1, C2; not Rs50), a figure glued to Rs/INR is parsed, and a bare four-digit number is a year only within 30 years before and 15 after the pack's week and in a year's context (a year word before it, a year word or no word after it); "the three months ended/to", "12 months ended", "trailing twelve months" and a month-day without a year are labels.
2026-09-25 M6 review R2-F5: config/staleness.yaml `fallback_of` (bse: nse): a fallback source isn't late while its primary is within its SLA (the digest table says "fallback, not needed"); the web app's banner follows the same file.
2026-09-25 M6 review R3-F1: with a router, P-05 checks every fact and why-mispriced item that passes the code checks (figures or not), given the cited items with their labels (a metric's name, period and unit; a signal's strength and named inputs) and the moves between cited periods, because a figure that equals some cited value can still name the wrong item, period or size; this replaces "M6 P-05" above (sentences without figures only). Code also checks "X, down/up from Y", "X versus Y" and "fell/rose to X" (a move into a cited period needs the period before it cited), and a change that isn't a level (a percent, or an amount after "by") takes the direction of the nearest movement verb in its clause; "tenfold" and "by a third" need a cited ratio.
2026-09-25 M6 review R3-F2..F5: after an abbreviation (Corp., Inc., Jr., St., U.S., dotted initials) a sentence ends only before a word that opens sentences (A, The, It, We, In, Revenue, Management, ...), and an ellipsis ends one before a capital; an amount written with a currency matches only cited money in that currency ("Rs", "euros", "C$" or "$" for a share count fail); a leading point (.95) is a figure, a four-digit number after "Q2 " is a year unless a lower-case word follows, and one before a capital is a figure unless a year word comes before it; "trailing 12-month", "out of 100" and "/100" are labels and "percentage points" a percent.
